{title: Away in a Manger}
{artist: Traditional / James R. Murray}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Carol}
{key: F}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 3/4}
{score: away-in-a-manger.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[F]way in a [Bb]manger, no [F]crib for a bed
The little Lord [C]Jesus laid [F]down His sweet head
The [F]stars in the [Bb]bright sky looked [F]down where He lay
The little Lord [C]Jesus a[F]sleep on the hay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [F]cattle are [Bb]lowing, the [F]baby awakes
But little Lord [C]Jesus no [F]crying He makes
I [F]love Thee, Lord [Bb]Jesus, look [F]down from the sky
And stay by my [C]cradle till [F]morning is nigh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Be [F]near me, Lord [Bb]Jesus, I [F]ask Thee to stay
Close by me for[C]ever, and [F]love me, I pray
Bless [F]all the dear [Bb]children in [F]Thy tender care
And fit us for [C]heaven, to [F]live with Thee there
{end_of_verse}
